<h1 id="the-do-catch-statement-in-swift">The do-catch Statement in Swift</h1>

<p>In Swift, the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">do-catch</code> statement is a mechanism for error handling. It allows you to execute code that might throw errors (in the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">do</code> block) and catch those errors (in the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">catch</code> block) for handling. This is an elegant way to handle runtime errors in Swift.</p>

<h2 id="example">Example</h2>

